          </table></div>
          <p>
            Two things stand out. The parts that fail most often, the key, the lubricant and the drive belt,
            are cheap. The ones that end a treadmill’s life, the motor, the control board and the console, can
            each cost a large share of what a budget machine sold for, before labour. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-repair-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill repair guide</a>
            covers diagnosis; this page is about buying the part once you know which it is.
          </p>
        </div>

