        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Find the model and serial number on the frame before anything else, and confirm the fault before you
            buy. Keys, lubricant and drive belts are cheap and fix more problems than their price suggests;
            boards, motors and consoles are where you need the maker’s part, matched by serial number, and where
            you should compare the repair with the cost of replacing the machine.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For NordicTrack and ProForm, go through iFIT; for Sole, its parts request form; for Precor, Precor or
            a dealer; for Life Fitness at home, customer support or an independent seller. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-repair-guide/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">treadmill repair guide</a>
            covers the diagnosis.
          </p>
